course: dictionary
lesson: 11492
title: Aggregate: the total
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aggregate is a formal word, but its main idea is simple: it means a total. When you see «aggregate», look for amounts being added together. «Mia added her scores from three games, and the aggregate was 45.» Mia added the scores, so aggregate means the total: 45.
explain: Sport uses aggregate in a special way. «The team lost the first game 1-0 but won the second 3-1, so they won on aggregate.» The winner is the team with the bigger total of both games added together, not the bigger score in one game. Ask yourself: what is being added up here?
explain: Aggregate can also be a word for things that are mixed together. Builders mix cement with «aggregate», which is sand and small stones. Try the swap check: if you put "total" in place of aggregate and it still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Aggregate means a total made by adding several amounts together.
fact: In sport, "on aggregate" means the total score over two or more games.
fact: As a verb, to aggregate means to collect or add things together into one total.
fact: In building, aggregate means sand, gravel and small stones mixed into concrete.
fact: Aggregate is a formal word, so it is often used in writing rather than in chatting with friends.
exercise: «Mia added her scores from three games. The aggregate was 45.» What does aggregate mean here? | A list of players' names | A single game score | A kind of sports ball | *A total made by adding amounts together
exercise: «The team lost the first game 1-0 but won the second 3-1, so they won on aggregate.» What does "on aggregate" mean? | The number of players on the pitch | *The total of both scores added together | The score of the last game only | Winning with no goals
exercise: In building, what is aggregate? | A kind of paint for walls | *Sand, gravel and small stones mixed into concrete | A tall tower of bricks | A tool for digging holes
test: Which phrase means the total of two games added together? | in the park | by hand | *on aggregate | at once
test: Which word means made up of many parts added together? | wobbly | hollow | tiny | *aggregate
exam: As a verb, aggregate means to: | *collect or add things together into one total | paint a wall | forget a score | split a total into smaller parts
